# zm's default box images (zm-eakh.12.23.6): what `zm host share` and `zm pool host` lend when no --image is
# given. zm embeds this file, so the pins update with zm. The daemon checks each box's booted digest against the
# binding's pin at acquire and releases any other (SPEC 20 "Boxes"), so a default is checked like any --image.
#
# Named images use name=NAME and are lent alone with --with NAME. host_default=on makes a named
# Tart image eligible as the default on hosts that meet min_host_macos; the newest compatible floor wins. root=on keeps passwordless sudo
# inside the VM by default (--root=false overrides it). Named images are not sandbox templates.
# One default line per layer and guest OS: layer, os, then the image pinned by digest (name@sha256:<64 hex>), or "-" when
# zm's own image for it is not published yet (share then says so and names --image), then the image's own floor
# when it has one (a published macOS Tart line must: ParsePins refuses it without): min_cpu=N min_memory_mb=N (a Tart
# image's cpuCountMin and memorySizeMin: tart set refuses less, so share lends no smaller size of it), and runner_dir=PATH when the image carries GitHub's runner (relative to the
# guest user's home unless absolute; zm-eakh.12.24.5): share binds it as the box's runner_dir, so the box serves
# GitHub Actions jobs (`github-jit`), and template=NAME on a template's line (zm-eakh.12.5.20): a layer's first
# line without one is its default, and share lends each published template image beside it (the default stays
# the binding's first image; `zm sandbox create --template NAME` boots the template's). A layer and OS have one
# plain line and one line per template; a template name is one internal/api knows (api.BoxTemplateImage). A box image needs sh, bash, awk, sleep, cat, kill, ps, perl, git, nc (and ip and ping for the VM-to-VM
# network check), plus what a GitHub just-in-time runner needs.
#
# tart darwin: Cirrus Labs' macOS Tahoe base, built from github.com/cirruslabs/macos-image-templates
#   (templates/vanilla-tahoe.pkr.hcl, then templates/base.pkr.hcl; MIT). It has the Tart guest agent, Homebrew
#   with the Command Line Tools (git), the GitHub runner in ~/actions-runner (scripts/install-actions-runner.sh,
#   run as the image's user admin), and macOS's own bash, perl, nc and
#   ping (no ip: the VM-to-VM check is a SKIP). macOS itself is under Apple's licence, which allows two macOS VMs
#   per Mac (zm-run-tart's cap). About 27 GB to pull. Digest of :latest read from ghcr.io on 2026-11-07; its Tart
#   config (the manifest's config layer) sets cpuCountMin 2 and memorySizeMin 4294967296 (4096 MiB).
# oci linux: zm's own, cmd/potluck-driver-tart/images/linux/Dockerfile (GitHub's actions-runner image plus netcat-openbsd,
#   iproute2, iputils-ping and procps; no public image has all of them). .github/workflows/box-images.yml
#   builds it, pushes ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-linux and writes its digest here (keeping the keys after it). The
#   runner is in /home/runner (the base's; the Dockerfile's build fails without /home/runner/run.sh).
# oci linux, template agent: zm's coding-agent image, cmd/potluck-driver-tart/images/agent/Dockerfile, built by the same
#   workflow FROM the potluck-box-linux image it pushes (so the runner and box tools stay), adding git, gh, Node 22
#   with npm and corepack, Go, Python 3 with pip and venv, ripgrep, jq, build-essential and the Claude Code and Codex
#   CLIs, each pinned. "-" until the workflow first publishes ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-agent.
# Compatibility policy: conservatively support Tahoe guests on Tahoe hosts, not on earlier hosts.
# ARM Linux uses Tart's macOS 13 host floor. These are support floors, not a claim about every
# possible Virtualization.framework combination; live exact-digest release checks remain required.
# arch and min_host_macos are mandatory for lending Tart digests; unknown compatibility refuses.
tart darwin ghcr.io/cirruslabs/macos-tahoe-base@sha256:65c3133a633fda8753cf1f71f2d55727792d534a2125b0032466563dcc8e58fd min_cpu=2 min_memory_mb=4096 runner_dir=actions-runner root=on min_free_gb=60 pull_minutes=60 pull_gb=27 min_host_macos=26 arch=arm64
# tart linux, name small-linux: Potluck's small Linux image for a Mac, what `potluck try` lends there first (docs/try.md), so a
#   first sandbox waits for about 1 GB, not macOS's 27. cmd/potluck-driver-tart/images/tart-linux/build.sh makes it on a
#   Mac from Cirrus Labs' Debian image (perl and git added, floor lowered to 1 vCPU and 2 GiB) and pushes it to
#   ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-tart-linux (public); write the digest it prints here. No GitHub runner.
tart linux ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-tart-linux@sha256:918d883297f39cb3da38d170b42c3cf1bb7876c5a8c616c136087529b8564589 name=small-linux min_cpu=1 min_memory_mb=2048 min_free_gb=10 pull_minutes=20 pull_gb=1 min_host_macos=13 arch=arm64
oci linux ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-linux@sha256:3fb0dddcbd97ae47bb40474c57d44f44cbdab337cb34e785c16f09d2235ccf3b runner_dir=/home/runner
oci linux ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-agent@sha256:0bd2cf0e52e9154a9a1a886a2ac44f652e5c45e599f32fe583212894cf2fb60c runner_dir=/home/runner template=agent
# Built by box-images run 43289820968 from its freshly published agent/Linux chain.
oci linux ghcr.io/sengirunners/potluck-box-browser@sha256:28b009beab77de08afbc02a1205085a4e595191f32198e4c8df3e164583b487e runner_dir=/home/runner template=browser
# min_free_gb budgets download, unpacked disk and box space; pull_minutes bounds the pull; pull_gb is about what a
# first pull downloads, for the words that warn of it.
# Named Mac image: selected alone by --with xcode, not as a sandbox template.
# Cirrus Xcode 26.3 (67.5 GB download, 120 GB disk); runner refreshed by the driver before each Actions job.
tart darwin ghcr.io/cirruslabs/macos-tahoe-xcode@sha256:39980f3a654be50fab35d8ead868b25b7b5c52adb59ec2fca23073c714cac9c6 min_cpu=2 min_memory_mb=4096 runner_dir=actions-runner root=on name=xcode min_free_gb=200 pull_minutes=180 pull_gb=68 min_host_macos=26 arch=arm64
# Sequoia alternative for macOS 15 hosts: upstream manifest/config inspected 2026-11-19.
# Digest 8386ef67, arm64/darwin, cpuCountMin=2, memorySizeMin=4294967296, 25.4 GB compressed.
# Host floor 15 is conservative Potluck policy; live exact-digest boot/isolation proof remains open.
tart darwin ghcr.io/cirruslabs/macos-sequoia-base@sha256:8386ef670c04b38e57bd0e97fe2cde6bc0598e1bcfba0212ecba1814e659a6b1 name=sequoia host_default=on min_host_macos=15 arch=arm64 min_cpu=2 min_memory_mb=4096 runner_dir=actions-runner root=on min_free_gb=60 pull_minutes=60 pull_gb=26
